# HwBinder service labels for vendor HALs.
#
# Entries transcribed from the stock 8.1 vendor
# /vendor/etc/selinux/nonplat_hwservice_contexts, restricted to interfaces
# that actually appear in the device manifest.xml (vendor.mediatek.hardware.*,
# vendor.oppo.hardware.*, vendor.silead.*, vendor.egistec.*, and
# vendor.qti.hardware.soter). Interfaces that exist in the stock policy but
# are not declared in this tree's manifest are omitted.
#
# Without these entries, every vendor HIDL service registers as
# default_hwservice, which the AOSP hwservicemanager allows but which makes
# the per-interface type transitions in device.te impossible. Under the
# bring-up permissive policy this only logs avc denials; on an enforcing
# build the HALs would be unable to find each other.
#
# The key format is <package>::<interface>, omitting the @version and
# instance suffix, matching the stock O-MR1 convention and every other
# HIDL entry in AOSP's vendor/hwservice_contexts.

