# --- Soter (Trustonic TEE) ---

# vendor.trustonic.soter@1.0-service (mtk_hal_soter) implements the
# vendor.qti.hardware.soter@1.0 HAL and registers its ISoter interface with
# hwservicemanager. The only client is SoterService
# (com.tencent.soter.soterserver), which runs in the system_app domain.
#
# IMPORTANT: keep this file's final newline. system/sepolicy/Android.mk defines
# an `add_nl` helper for exactly this case ("allow OEM policy configuration
# files without a final newline (0x0A) to be built correctly by the m4(1) macro
# processor"), but hwservice_contexts.mk does not apply it -- it hands the raw
# file list straight to m4. Without the trailing newline, m4 fuses this file's
# last line into the first line of the next contexts file (LineageOS's
# vendor.lineage.biometrics.fingerprint.inscreen), and checkfc dies with:
#   invalid MLS context s0vendor.lineage.biometrics.fingerprint.inscreen::IFingerprintInscreen
vendor.qti.hardware.soter::ISoter	u:object_r:hal_soter_hwservice:s0
